 {color:#3c763d}*2064175360*{color}

Hey [~accountid:610a3ee66051c5006aeeeea1] thank you for your help! 

Find our answers below : 

{color:#006644}*Do we have a way to notify Riders that we are collecting this amount in accordance with our T&Cs and because of breach of parking requirements (just before or at the time of the money collection)?*{color}{color:#006644} {color}

Yesterday, I issued a fine to [~accountid:638713ee77acd224b3411ff9] , and he received the following notification. We can run a test by adjusting the settings for PT and verify what notification the user receives if we charge immediately.

!image-20250212-160950.png|width=1320,height=2868,alt="image-20250212-160950.png"!

{color:#006644}*In order to better understand the situation, and keep track of this topic (that has ben ongoing since 2022), can I please ask you to clarify your proposal here:*{color}

* {color:#006644}*how much would you like to charge to Riders*{color}
* {color:#006644}*when*{color}
* {color:#006644}*in which situation*{color}
* {color:#006644}*why this change of plans now (backlog or anything else)?*{color}
* {color:#006644}*etc*{color}

PM and EMEL fines: We want to pass on parking fines to our users in cases where vehicles have been incorrectly parked. The amount charged will include the fine, towing fee, and daily fee, which can be €73, €79, or €82, depending on the year. We will apply this to all fines under these conditions since 2023.

As seen in our test with Frederico, the fine is not currently charged immediately. There is a risk that the user may remove their payment method, making it impossible to collect the amount. For this reason, we would like to understand if there is a legal basis to charge the fine immediately and avoid the risk.

{color:#006644}*+* {color}[~accountid:626fb920f42962006fde4c04]{color:#006644} *mentioned that he believes some contractual penalties (e.g. the "parking enforcement fee" for failing to take an end of ride photo of a legally parked scooter) are collected immediately, however the user has advanced notice of this on the end of ride screen, whereas for a so called "city fine" this arrives weeks/months later... →Pls clarify this as well.*{color}

If the user parks in a no go area where parking and riding are not allowed, they receive a fine immediately in the app. The municipal police fine arrives at our office much later.

In this [Legal|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1w83azRVr0KsNsH4PXg-hOnIhSxrJ2Vxt/edit] Memo prepared by SPASS we asked *“Can we charge the penalties without prior notice or warning to the user? As mentioned above, we believe that if we warn users in advance, they will change their primary payment method and make it impossible for us to charge the penalty.”* and their reply was *“It just needs to be in the T&Cs, which users will accept.”* Considering sections 5.7.5 and 5.10 of our T&Cs, is this covered?

_5.7.5 is not parked in accordance with section 3.1 of the Driving Rules set out in ANNEX A to this Agreement, then we may charge you a penalty of up to EUR 680 (‘Parking Penalty’). You agree that improper parking is a breach of this Agreement and acknowledge that the imposition of the Parking Penalty is a reasonable and necessary measure to ensure the proper use of parking areas, public spaces and the safety and well-being of other users and the general public;_

_5.10 You agree to pay any fines, fees, penalties, and/or any other charges incurred by us, resulting from your use of any E-Vehicle, your improper parking of any (E-vehicle - This seems to be a typo in the T&C) (e.g., outside a Permitted Parking Area), or as a result of violating any law, rule, regulation, or ordinance while using the Services._

!image-20250212-163641.png|width=1310,height=270,alt="image-20250212-163641.png"!

Let me know if this answers all your questions, please. And again, thank you!

