Hey [~accountid:610a3ee66051c5006aeeeea1],

When a user is riding and deliberately tries to stop in a no-go zone, the app warns them that proceeding will result in a fine. This fine is usually around €10 but can be adjusted on admin.

If a user parks outside a designated parking spot without receiving a warning from the app, either because they abandoned the vehicle without ending the ride or parked within the buffer zone but outside the actual parking space, the OPS team selects some cases randomly and issues a micro fine. This fine is typically up to €2 but can go as high as €6.

{color:#006644}*Do you know if this corresponds to clause 5.7.1 of our T&Cs:*{color}
{color:#006644}*_"If it is parked outside the Authorised Parking Area, we may charge a collection fee of up to 100 euros. This amount is based on our collection costs and associated losses.”_*{color}

Clause 5.7.1 seems to refer to this, as “collection costs and associated losses” likely cover rebalancing and collecting vehicles to keep the city organised.

{color:#006644}*What amount do we charge? if it’s aligned with the above, it should be 100 euros*{color}
If this aligns with clause 5.7.1, then theoretically, we could charge up to €100. However, since the clause states “up to,” charging €2, €6, or €10 should not be an issue.

{color:#006644}*When do we charge it on the rider’s account? immediately, or do we send them a notification first?*{color}
Yes, the fine is deducted from the user’s account immediately.

{color:#006644}*What kind of message or in-app notification does the rider receives and when?*{color}
The message is customised by us. Generally, we inform the user that a fine has been issued.

{color:#006644}*Since when have we been doing this in PT?*{color}
We started issuing these fines in mid-2023.

{color:#006644}*To how many riders (roughly) have we been charging this?*{color}
Approximately 2,000 fines have been issued.

*Are you aware of any complaints in that respect?*
Yes, we have received some SC tickets related to this.

