Hi all - jumping in on this from the Privacy POV. Hopefully this should address some of your outstanding questions.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Driver Selfie Verification*
{panel}

As mentioned below, we should be fine to launch this in BE, *_provided that_* it adheres to the same process / flow as in other jurisdictions. This is because we have previously advised on collecting explicit consent when scanning a driver’s image, as well as other elements of this process, and we need to make sure that the same compliance steps are taken in BE both to ensure consistency and to make sure we are not exposing Bolt to unnecessary risk.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Audio Trip Recording*
{panel}

The reason we have asked about how much demand there is for ATR is as follows:

* Before launching ATR in any country, we need to perform a local law analysis. The reason for this analysis is that audio recording is a sensitive feature, and in a number of countries it is forbidden to record audio without consent, or without informing the persons recorded. In some countries, breaching the obligations re audio recording are a criminal offence. 
* We have not previously performed an analysis for Belgium, and we haven't been informed about the need/initiative to launch ATR in Belgium. Therefore, if there is a *_pressing need_* for a full analysis of ATR feasibility for Belgium, please let me know, as we would need to plan our budget / resources for this (i.e., it will take a few weeks and we would need to engage local counsel).

