*Dashcams*
{panel}

The reason why I am hesitant on offering discounts to drivers is as follows:

* From a privacy POV, we have taken the position that drivers are independent controllers of any footage recorded on their dashcams - this position allows us to sidestep a lot of privacy law issues that would otherwise arise, and is one we recently reiterated to the Estonian regulator. In order to be able to maintain this position, *we need to be able to demonstrate that we do not exercise any control over the use of the cameras*.
* As you have noted, providing drivers with dashcams to install in their cars could be interpreted as Bolt trying to exercise a form of control, which is why we avoid it. Although offering discounts to drivers when purchasing dashcams is a step away from this, it still *flirts with the same issues*.
* If there is a pressing need for offering discounts on dashcams, then *this is something we can do, provided that we are willing to accept the risks* that come with it. [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] did you previously review this in FR and green-light it provided we review the agreements? If so I am happy to take the same appriach to ensure consistency.

